# given-up-after-the-cascade

The collections service is down, so alice's closure runs out of patience and is given back. 
Bob takes his own meme down at some moment during it, and alice's comment hangs under that 
meme. The compensation can only return what it is still holding — and the question is 
whether that is the same thing on every order of the same events. 

search: exhaustive — every schedule this transport allows was walked
distinct end states: 2

[A]
    identity was told: [PORTAL_PURGE_FAILED]
    the parts confirmed: {alice/comments=1, alice/memes=0}
    still on the wire: [content-commands→collections PURGE_USER_CONTENT → collections, content-commands→collections PURGE_USER_CONTENT → collections, content-commands→collections PURGE_USER_CONTENT → collections, content-commands→collections PURGE_USER_CONTENT → collections, content-commands→collections RESTORE_USER_CONTENT → collections]
    rows: the portal holds nothing at all

[B]
    identity was told: [PORTAL_PURGE_FAILED]
    the parts confirmed: {alice/comments=0, alice/memes=0}
    still on the wire: [content-commands→collections PURGE_USER_CONTENT → collections, content-commands→collections PURGE_USER_CONTENT → collections, content-commands→collections PURGE_USER_CONTENT → collections, content-commands→collections PURGE_USER_CONTENT → collections, content-commands→collections RESTORE_USER_CONTENT → collections]
    rows: the portal holds nothing at all

